Thus both default/custom renames should work.

**R3**: After successful rename, getAllCategories must no longer list old category name. Implementation: renameCategory updates rename mapping for default categories (`data.rename[defaultMatch] = newName`) or replaces custom name in data.custom. getAllCategories returns each category: defaults loops over DEFAULT_CATEGORIES, uses data.rename[def] ?? def to produce name; but note: For renamed default, it adds a result entry with id = def, name = renamed (newName). The original name (def) is not in final result (name) but id field equals def. In tests, getAllCategories returns array of objects each with name property (the visible category). The test asserts categories.find(c => c.name === 'Meals') toBeUndefined; categories.find(c => c.name === 'Food & Dining') toBeDefined. That passes. Fine.

